  "superseded": "The flow scores in this study are wrong: the case’s gauge line (2026-11-06) spanned only the creek channel, and on these storms part of the flood crossed the floodplain north of it uncounted (a line across the whole valley read 2.0 times the volume on 10 August 2023). The level errors stand. Combined-sewer mode was on in every run (the case files carried it, with downspouts 100 % to the sewer, though Charlotte’s storm sewers are separate): pipe ends the outfall layer missed took their water out of the model, and on 12 June 2025 the gauge saw under half the flow. Superseded by the studies of 2026-11-08."
